      "title": "How this workflow works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Audio8 voice tags\n\nThe two Audio8 Voice Set Add nodes build a free tag -> voice dictionary. The tag string is arbitrary; it has no relationship to the voice file name. A duplicate tag is kept automatically as tag_1, tag_2, ... (see the log output of the Add node).\n\nIn the Audio8 Script text, [happy] switches the voice reference until the next tag. Text before the first tag uses the reference input of Audio8 TTS. [[ and ]] write literal brackets. Unknown [...] brackets stay in the spoken text and are listed as warnings in the log output. Tag boundaries are treated like paragraph pauses (paragraph_pause_ms).\n\nThe preset names Barbara_Happy / Barbara_Sad only exist on this machine. Create your own presets with Audio8 Encode Reference plus Audio8 Save Voice, then pick them in the two Load Voice nodes.\n\nKnown limitation: preset loudness carries over as-is; there is no volume normalisation between voices."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Audio8 voice tags\n\nThe two Audio8 Voice Set Add nodes build a free tag -> voice dictionary. The tag string is arbitrary; it has no relationship to the voice file name. A duplicate tag is kept automatically as tag_1, tag_2, ... (see the log output of the Add node).\n\nIn the Audio8 Script text, [happy] switches the voice reference until the next tag. Text before the first tag uses the reference input of Audio8 TTS. [[ and ]] write literal brackets. Unknown [...] brackets stay in the spoken text and are listed as warnings in the log output. Tag boundaries are treated like paragraph pauses (paragraph_pause_ms).\n\nThe preset names Barbara_Happy / Barbara_Sad only exist on this machine. Create your own presets with Audio8 Encode Reference plus Audio8 Save Voice, then pick them in the two Load Voice nodes.\n\nKnown limitation: preset loudness carries over as-is; there is no volume normalisation between voices."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
